    <string name="help_text">P — how far your heart rate swings within one breath, peak minus trough, in beats per minute. A breath that takes you from 62 to 71 beats/min is a swing of 9. The resonance-breathing signal itself.\n\nRhythm — how much of that swing is a clean sine at the pacer\'s rate (0–100 %). Depth without rhythm earns little lift.\n\nSteady — the swing is there, but it does not follow the pacer. Breathe with the bar, at the same speed, with no pauses. Do not breathe deeper.\n\nLift — P between the lift threshold and the sky ceiling, scaled by rhythm. A star falls for each 10 s that the balloon stays at the ceiling. Stars come only from a live estimate.\n\nTrace — your heart rate over the last 30 s. Light bands are inhales, dark bands exhales; the band at the right edge is the breath you are in.\n\nStars — Ranks compare the number of stars earned in each session. Sessions rank after 2 min of valid signal; equal star totals are ordered newest first.\n\nSearch score — median of P × rhythm over the six measured breaths of a probe, used to compare breathing rates during a resonance search.\n\nBreathe gently and comfortably; do not force deeper breaths to lift the balloon. Stop pacing if you feel dizzy or uncomfortable. The strap does not measure breathing depth or carbon dioxide.\n\nFind my resonance rate — a separate search mode that tries rates between 4 and 7 /min during one 15-min session (9 breaths each) and picks the one with the biggest, cleanest swing. It only reports a rate when its estimate has settled; with no clear peak it ends at the 5.5 /min default. The card shows the model\'s peak (the rate it would pick) next to the single best probe; they can differ by a step.</string>
